<article class="env-lemma" id="02VB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02VB">Lemma <span data-tag="02VB">39.18.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. Let $g : U' \to U$ be a morphism of schemes. Consider the following diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ R' \ar[d] \ar[r] \ar@/_3pc/[dd]_{t'} \ar@/^1pc/[rr]^{s'}&  R \times _{s, U} U' \ar[r] \ar[d] &  U' \ar[d]^ g \\  U' \times _{U, t} R \ar[d] \ar[r] &  R \ar[r]^ s \ar[d]_ t &  U \\  U' \ar[r]^ g &  U }  \]
</div>
  <p> where all the squares are fibre product squares. Then there is a canonical composition law $c' : R' \times _{s', U', t'} R' \to R'$ such that $(U', R', s', t', c')$ is a groupoid scheme over $S$ and such that $U' \to U$, $R' \to R$ defines a morphism $(U', R', s', t', c') \to (U, R, s, t, c)$ of groupoid schemes over $S$. Moreover, for any scheme $T$ over $S$ the functor of groupoids </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (U'(T), R'(T), s', t', c') \to (U(T), R(T), s, t, c)  \]
</div>
  <p> is the restriction (see above) of $(U(T), R(T), s, t, c)$ via the map $U'(T) \to U(T)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
